=== routed MoE rows kernels, reduced dimension swept (group 32, 16 experts/tile, r=1, 50 iterations) ===
Blocks of 8 groups run 32 lanes wide; leftover groups run one at a
time on 16 lanes. `trips` = blocks + tail = inner-loop iterations.
If the kernel is paid per byte, `us/group` is flat and `us/trip` is
not. If it is paid per trip, the reverse -- and the sweep is a saw.
GB/s is weight traffic against the 135 GB/s floor 20-M4.8 §3 measured
on the dense k-row kernels (461 MB in 3.41 ms).

